abstract: >
  HERESY v7.0.0 HERESY/360 is a deterministic hosted account-decision operating environment
  whose primary stack is implemented in Ada, Fortran and COBOL. Ada performs case admission
  and deterministic case-ID generation, Fortran applies explicit due-process invariants and a
  mechanical completeness score, and COBOL renders the user-facing decision receipt. A POSIX
  shell layer provides local orchestration. The reference policy refuses adverse enforcement
  when a specific rule or evidence reference is missing, exposes explicit remediation or human
  review routing, performs no network access or model inference, and emits deterministic receipts.
  A local fictional demo is inspired by the interface failure of an automated support notice that
  says "specifically:" without supplying a specific rule; the software does not connect to or
  adjudicate any real platform account.
